<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Schalksburg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Schalksburg was a castle on a hill near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balingen">Balingen</a> and Albstadt in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swabian-jura">Swabian Jura</a>, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. From the late thirteenth century it was the seat of a branch of the counts of Zollern, the Schalksburg line, whose lordship included Balingen. In 1403 the last count of this line sold the lordship to Württemberg. Only ruins remain.</p></div>
